Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:27:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] [M156] FSA: restrict */.git writes to an allowlist of
 safe repository paths

Original change's description:
> FSA: restrict */.git writes to an allowlist of safe repository paths
>
> GenerateBlockPaths() previously registered separate kBlockWrite suffix
> rules for .git/hooks, .git/config, and .git/modules, which did not cover
> creating a .git directory or gitfile pointer directly or writing other
> configuration/indirection metadata such as .git/commondir or
> .git/worktrees/*/commondir.
>
> Replace those three suffix rules with a single */.git kBlockWrite rule
> and delegate write checks under */.git to ShouldBlockAccessToGitPath().
> That helper blocks .git creation and sensitive metadata by default
> (including config*, hooks, modules, commondir, worktrees, info, and
> objects/info), while allowlisting repository data, ref, and index paths
> under an existing .git directory so web-based Git clients continue to
> work without weakening stricter ancestor or nested suffix rules.
>
> Fixed: 577352729, 576861549, 577139798, 577455555, 576632066
